---
import { getCollection } from "astro:content";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import ArticleCard from "../components/ArticleCard.astro";

const articles = (await getCollection("articles"))
  .sort((a, b) => b.data.pubDate.valueOf() - a.data.pubDate.valueOf());

const featured = articles.filter((article) => article.data.featured);
const featuredForHome = featured.slice(0, 3);
const featuredIds = new Set(featuredForHome.map((article) => article.id));
const latest = articles.filter((article) => !featuredIds.has(article.id)).slice(0, 6);
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Global Food Crisis Report | Food Supply, Prices & Solutions"
  description="Evidence-led global food crisis reporting on supply, prices, shortages and food security, with 2026–27 outlooks, practical solutions and recovery signals."
>
  <section class="hero hero-home">
    <div class="shell hero-grid">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">Global Food Supply Intelligence</p>
        <h1>The Global Food Supply, Explained.</h1>
        <p>We track food-supply risks, price shocks, agricultural pressures and food-security conditions — then explain the causes, evidence and practical solutions.</p>
        <div class="hero-actions">
          <a class="button button-primary" href="#latest">Read the latest</a>
          <a class="button button-secondary" href="#explore">Explore topics</a>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="callout">
        <strong>How we report:</strong> A local shortage, a price increase, a forecast or a stockpiling episode is not automatically evidence of a worldwide food shortage. We label what is verified, forecast and analysed.
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="current-evidence">
    <div class="shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">Current evidence snapshot</p>
      <h2>What the latest global data does—and does not—say</h2>
      <p>Snapshot based on FAO releases published 6 November 2026. These indicators point to a mixed picture: high aggregate cereal output and rising global stocks, falling international prices in October, uneven commodity movements and persistent acute food needs in several regions.</p>
      <div class="card-grid">
        <article class="card">
          <h3>International food prices</h3>
          <p>FAO’s Food Price Index averaged 133.9 points in October, down 1.2% from September but 5.9% above October 2025. The headline hides differences between commodities.</p>
          <p><a href="https://www.fao.org/newsroom/detail/fao-food-price-index-edges-down-in-october-amid-subdued-demand/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read FAO’s 6 November price release</a></p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Global cereal production</h3>
          <p>FAO’s November estimate puts 2026 cereal production at 2,999 million tonnes, the second-highest level on record. Rice production is forecast at 552 million tonnes, 2.5% lower year over year.</p>
          <p><a href="https://www.fao.org/worldfoodsituation/csdb/en/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read the November cereal brief</a></p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Stocks and trade</h3>
          <p>World cereal stocks are forecast to rise 1.8%, with a 32.4% stocks-to-use ratio. Global cereal trade is forecast to fall 3.3% to 507.7 million tonnes.</p>
          <p><a href="https://www.fao.org/worldfoodsituation/csdb/en/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Check the supply-and-demand tables</a></p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Acute food needs</h3>
          <p>FAO identifies 41 countries or territories requiring external food assistance, 31 of them in Africa. Conflict and insecurity remain major drivers; this measure is not a global famine classification.</p>
          <p><a href="https://doi.org/10.4060/ce2428en" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read FAO’s crop prospects report</a></p>
        </article>
      </div>
      <p class="small-note">This is a dated evidence snapshot, not a live feed or a prediction. Commodity forecasts can be revised; follow the linked original releases for newer data and methodology.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">How to use this site</p>
      <h2>Check a food-crisis claim in three steps</h2>
      <div class="card-grid">
        <article class="card"><h3>1. Define the claim</h3><p>Separate a price increase, a temporary stock-out, a harvest forecast and a confirmed humanitarian emergency.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>2. Match the source to the question</h3><p>Use production and stocks data for availability, price data for costs, and WFP or IPC assessments for acute food insecurity.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>3. Check the date and location</h3><p>Record when the data was published and whether it applies to the whole world, a country, or a specific region.</p></article>
      </div>
      <p>Start with our <a href="/articles/food-collapse-fact-check-2026/">food-collapse fact check</a>, review the <a href="/sources/">source directory</a>, or read our <a href="/editorial-policy/">editorial policy</a> to understand how claims are handled.</p>
      <p>Planning a household food budget? Use the <a href="/food-budget-calculator/">food budget scenario calculator</a> to test how a hypothetical price change could affect your monthly grocery spending.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="start-here">
    <div class="shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">Start with your question</p>
      <h2>Global food crisis: key questions and practical answers</h2>
      <div class="card-grid">
        <article class="card"><h3><a href="/articles/global-food-crisis-2026/">Is there a global food crisis?</a></h3><p>Check the latest evidence on production, food prices, stocks, trade and regional hunger.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3><a href="/articles/how-can-world-prevent-food-crisis-10-solutions/">Food security solutions</a></h3><p>Ten practical measures, emergency distribution guidance and a food crisis management plan.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3><a href="/articles/food-prices-2027-forecast-scenarios/">Food shortage 2027: risk list</a></h3><p>Seven risks to monitor, with the evidence that would confirm or weaken each concern.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3><a href="/articles/when-will-food-crisis-end-2026/">When will the food crisis end?</a></h3><p>Five measurable recovery signals for prices, harvests, trade, inputs and food access.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {featuredForHome.length > 0 && (
    <section class="section">
      <div class="shell">
        <p class="eyebrow">Featured analysis</p>
        <div class="card-grid">
          {featuredForHome.map((article) => <ArticleCard article={article} featured />)}
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  )}


  <section class="section section-featured" id="latest">
    <div class="shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">Latest</p>
      <h2>Latest food-supply reporting and explainers</h2>
      {latest.length ? (
        <div class="card-grid">
          {latest.map((article) => <ArticleCard article={article} />)}
        </div>
      ) : (
        <div class="card"><p>The first evidence-based articles are being prepared.</p></div>
      )}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-explore" id="explore">
    <div class="shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">Explore</p>
      <h2>Follow the drivers behind food-supply risk</h2>
      <div class="card-grid">
        <div class="card"><h3><a href="/global-food-crisis/">Global Food Crisis</a></h3><p>Global availability, hunger, food insecurity and major risk factors.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3><a href="/food-supply/">Food Supply</a></h3><p>Grain, rice, stocks, imports, exports and production.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3><a href="/food-security/">Food Security</a></h3><p>Food access, affordability, hunger, stability and resilience.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3><a href="/food-shortages/">Food Shortages</a></h3><p>Localized shortages, availability disruptions and the evidence behind shortage claims.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3><a href="/food-prices/">Food Prices</a></h3><p>Commodity prices, inflation, fuel, freight and household impact.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3><a href="/supply-chain/">Supply Chain</a></h3><p>Shipping, ports, trade routes, storage and logistics disruptions.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3><a href="/fertilizer/">Fertilizer</a></h3><p>Fertilizer prices, availability, trade and nutrient efficiency.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3><a href="/water-food/">Water & Food</a></h3><p>Drought, irrigation, groundwater and agricultural water stress.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3><a href="/climate-agriculture/">Climate & Agriculture</a></h3><p>El Niño, drought, heat, rainfall and crop resilience.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3><a href="/food-storage/">Food Storage & Stockpiling</a></h3><p>Preparedness, household storage, shelf life and stockpiling behavior.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3><a href="/countries/">Countries</a></h3><p>Country-by-country food-security and food-supply conditions.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3><a href="/solutions/">Solutions</a></h3><p>Evidence-based measures that can strengthen resilient food systems.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
